 labeling refers to the practice of providing information about the nutritional content of food products to help consumers make informed choices. This includes details about various dietary attributes, such as gluten content, enabling individuals to better understand the nutritional value and ingredients of the foods they consume.", "CONSUMO ALIMENTARIO:Consumo alimentario refers to the act of consuming food, which is linked to health and the preparation of meals at home.", "ETIQUETADO NUTRICIONAL:The entity \"ETIQUETADO NUTRICIONAL\" refers to nutritional labeling, which encompasses the regulations and information presented on food packaging. This labeling is designed to inform consumers about the nutritional content of food products, helping them make informed dietary choices.", "REGLAMENTO (UE) Nº 1169/2011:Reglamento (UE) Nº 1169/2011 is a legal framework established by the European Parliament and Council that governs the information related to food that must be provided to consumers. This regulation aims to ensure that consumers receive clear and accurate information about the food products they purchase, thereby promoting informed choices and enhancing food safety.", "ALIMENTOS ENVASADOS:Packaged foods are those that are sealed before sale, requiring clear labeling of their contents.", "PRODUCTOS ALIMENTARIOS:Food products are items that are consumed and require clear labeling to inform consumers about their nutritional content.", "ETIQUETADO:ETIQUETADO refers to the labeling process that encompasses the information required to be present on food products, particularly those with very low caloric content, as mandated by regulations. This includes adherence to specific norms that govern the information displayed on food items, especially concerning allergens. Additionally, ETIQUETADO involves providing essential details such as the minimum durability date and nutritional information, which aids consumers in understanding the contents and nutritional value of the food they purchase. Overall, ETIQUETADO plays a crucial role in ensuring transparency and safety in food labeling.", "REAL DECRETO 1245/2008:El Real Decreto 1245/2008 es una legislación española que regula la información sobre los aditivos alimentarios y su etiquetado.", "EMPRESA ALIMENTARIA:La empresa alimentaria es la entidad responsable de la producción y etiquetado de productos alimenticios, incluyendo la información sobre ingredientes y alérgenos.", "CONSUMIDORES:Los consumidores son las personas que compran y consumen productos alimenticios, y tienen derecho a recibir información clara sobre los mismos.", "PRODUCTOS ALIMENTICIOS:Los productos alimenticios son bienes que se consumen y que deben cumplir con regulaciones específicas sobre etiquetado y seguridad alimentaria."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}